        "sender_full_name": "Jonas Bayer",
        "timestamp": 1782298537
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Sorry didnt mean to smudge my comments into the code like that (of course you willjust copypaste the block, still learning here).   Uhh... I probably messed up when I copied the command  lines in one by one, and missed one of those add_assoc calls, but either way I am at the final step where I have the output I posted, and the game just hangs when I try to execute rfl.  Maybe its just a server issue, I will retry to input the level from scratch, thanks Jonas.</p>\n<p>Yeah, it went through that time..  I don't know, the server keeps hanging up on me if I spend too long thinking, maybe that is the problem.  I had refreshed it when I was having the problem the first time.</p>",
        "id": 606211327,
        "sender_full_name": "Ian Allen",
        "timestamp": 1782298764
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think easily the hardest part of all of these is fiddling with the parenthesis and the order of terms.  For example, I've got </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and I cannot for the life of me, figure out how to use add_comm to flip (b*d + b).  Is it even possible yet?  I am on stage 8/9 and suspect it has something to do with x * y + b not being the same type as  a + b, even if you have x*y = a, which I dont actually get to declare yet on this stage I think..</p>",
        "id": 606219997,
        "sender_full_name": "Ian Allen",
        "timestamp": 1782301891
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You can write <code>rw [add_comm (b*d) b]</code> or <code>nth_rw 6 [add_comm]</code> (prefer the first one though)</p>",
