    {
        "content": "<p>After the rewrite sequence, the goal reduces to a reflexive equality:</p>\n<p>a + (a + (1 + 1)) = a + (a + (1 + 1))</p>\n<p>At this point the two sides are syntactically identical, so <code>rfl</code> closes the goal.</p>\n<p>My remaining question is not how to close the proof, but whether there is a cleaner way to structure these arithmetic rewrites.</p>",
        "id": 606258973,
        "sender_full_name": "Salkutsan Aleksey",
        "timestamp": 1782310622
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've gotten past the multiplication section but yeah, the way lean parses those statements implicitly is not super clear (at least to me) as a new user.   Even when mousing over the operators to see the parenthesis (which is clear enough), it seems to have some particular expectations about the allowable type when applying the early lemmas.   Things like if succ_mul or mul_succ apply, when inside parenthesis.  I would expect that to always work but it certainly doesn't.  That or it's just the game/server bugging out somehow.  </p>\n<p>These later sections are much easier.</p>\n<p>Salkutsan those questions don't seem to be directed at me, I assume, so I haven't answered you..(and can't).</p>\n<p>Ok there's maybe something wrong with the game?  Im doing the power section and all the intro text is missing for subsections 3, 4, and 5 so far.   subsection 6 has \"Let's now begin our approach to the final boss, by proving some more subtle facts about powers.\" but nothing else. ...or maybe thats how its supposed to look.</p>",
