    {
        "content": "<p>I found a little bug I think.  On level 5/6 Advanced Addition World, I can </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">case</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span>\n<span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">add_zero</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"n\">exact</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and this both solves the intermediate goal and fails as a command simultaneously, resulting in the output</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">Failed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"n\">exact</span>\n<span class=\"n\">intermediate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">solved!</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"n\">fruitbasket</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span>\n<span class=\"n\">unexpected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">input</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I only typed exact because the previous solutions shown in 4/6 on completion used this command instead of trivial.</p>",
